                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3f06f05e-7b24-4569-8bda-82b5130adcee",
                        "entry_id": "fde6174c-e262-3135-9001-70e0163fadb2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "salutaires"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "28f33a90-4211-32aa-91a5-142a0f87320d",
                        "entry_id": "fde6174c-e262-3135-9001-70e0163fadb2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est utile, avantageux pour la conservation de la vie, de la santé, des biens, de l’honneur, pour le salut de l’âme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "000dd01e-0378-4021-85d2-b410b9d3d658",
                                "sense_id": "28f33a90-4211-32aa-91a5-142a0f87320d",
                                "text": "Lorsque cette discussion médicale fut terminée, le paysan saxon demanda humblement qu’on lui restituât le remède qui lui avait été si salutaire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "603e539b-a146-4356-a2d3-fc93f46b7969",
                                "sense_id": "28f33a90-4211-32aa-91a5-142a0f87320d",
                                "text": "…toutefois comme il ne voulait pas abandonner dans les eaux de la tribulation le jeune paroissien de son confrère, il lui donna quelques salutaires encouragements."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17e54065-16de-4d0a-9add-513db2f6a06e",
                                "sense_id": "28f33a90-4211-32aa-91a5-142a0f87320d",
                                "text": "Jadis le sorcier, le magicien, le jeteur de sort faisaient grand usage du crapaud. On recourait à ses pouvoirs maléfiques ou salutaires."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95ac786e-dcf5-42ee-abc9-5445729da229",
                                "sense_id": "28f33a90-4211-32aa-91a5-142a0f87320d",
                                "text": "…il y a eu, sur ces rives du Tarn, une petite patrie autonome, très florissante, très fière, à laquelle, convenons-en, l'autorité centralisatrice venue du Nord n'a point été salutaire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c6eea9ba-91a0-4135-804b-4982d9bb45df",
                        "source_entry_id": "fde6174c-e262-3135-9001-70e0163fadb2",
                        "source_sense_id": "28f33a90-4211-32aa-91a5-142a0f87320d",
                        "target_lang_word": "salutary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "salutary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67173325-e062-3be1-9516-943a29b3dd5d",
                                        "entry_id": "389a0060-99d7-364b-afdb-e7d36c13a004",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Effecting or designed to effect an improvement; remedial."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e09f6461-3e01-4bec-a740-c676bb8d4447",
                                                "sense_id": "67173325-e062-3be1-9516-943a29b3dd5d",
                                                "text": "salutary advice"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf2d5696-f430-4544-836d-a75a554ccedd",
                                                "sense_id": "67173325-e062-3be1-9516-943a29b3dd5d",
                                                "text": "The effect was most salutary; and, amid starts and screams—for the poor girl was fairly frightened out of the small portion of sense that, at any time, belonged to her—they learned that Lord Marchmont had been found dead in his bed; and that Lady Marchmont was, with the shock, in a state of almost insanity!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cfab52a-b7ab-4bc6-872d-a17bbdf762d5",
                                                "sense_id": "67173325-e062-3be1-9516-943a29b3dd5d",
                                                "text": "We do it here historically, and I think it's, um, very salutary to know quite a bit about the history of ideas, particularly in philosophy which always suffers from a tendency to follow the latest fashion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7148a961-d2dc-46fc-a392-dfecacc42d00",
                                                "sense_id": "67173325-e062-3be1-9516-943a29b3dd5d",
                                                "text": "Using such neofuturists as Nicholas Negroponte to support his argument, Groper argues that “being digital” is constitutive of today’s salutary political life (167)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b6dd048-be82-3ef8-b461-277c22b026dc",
                                        "entry_id": "389a0060-99d7-364b-afdb-e7d36c13a004",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Promoting good health and physical well-being; wholesome; curative."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e023540c-7fe1-4c46-9a68-48b150fe0787",
                                                "sense_id": "6b6dd048-be82-3ef8-b461-277c22b026dc",
                                                "text": "In the living state, the body is observed to […] reject what is noxious; to select what is salutary; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
